{"availability":"available","full":"indiesoftby/defold-sharp-sprite","name":"defold-sharp-sprite","description":"Rotated Grid Super-Sampling (RGSS) for the Defold engine.","category":"Other","language":"GLSL","stars":78,"forks":3,"created":"2020-11-16T16:55:14Z","updated":"2025-06-10T19:43:44Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://indiesoftby.github.io/defold-sharp-sprite/","topics":["defold","defold-game-engine","defold-library","defold-shaders"],"demo":"https://indiesoftby.github.io/defold-sharp-sprite/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:07.068Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:07.068Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:07.068Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T20:15:07.068Z","stars":78,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Sharp Sprite is the implementation of Rotated Grid Super-Sampling (RGSS) for the Defold engine. If you use down-scaled high-resolution images in your game and you want to get rid of blurriness (because of mipmapping) or sharpness (because of disabled mipmapping), then RGSS is for you.","How does it work? RGSS samples the texture multiple times with an offset on each sample and averages the results. For this, it uses a 4x MSAA rotated grid pattern, sometimes called 4 rooks.","The second solution, that included in this repo, uses mip biasing. Mip biasing tells the GPU to adjust what mip level to use. The shaders use mip bias of -1.0 that pushes the mip level one full mip back to make 2D sprites look much sharper."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/indiesoftby/defold-sharp-sprite/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7fe8c381f450bcd0e8f8ee4f86771dea21ba61a911bb083dc030eb91ae304938","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:07.197Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:07.197Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Sharp Sprite is the implementation of Rotated Grid Super-Sampling (RGSS) for the Defold engine. If you use down-scaled high